// A NULLABLE REF value in an INFERRED struct field. `vl check` returns 0 and the emitter
// refused with `emitProgram: ref valtype with no interned shape` — the field needs an
// interned wrapper shape, and the mint that reads the literal coded a niche nullable -1, so
// the whole literal got no row at all and its global cell had no struct slot to name.
//
// Not closure-specific: a nullable string, struct, list or ref-list field takes the same
// route, while a nullable `i32` field always ran because its niche is the value-union box
// and needs no shape. The annotated field runs at every rep, a non-nullable closure field
// runs, and the same value bound as a local runs — so the ingredients were the field being
// INFERRED and its value being a nullable REF. The frame-scoped spelling reached a different
// floor (`object literal but no struct type declared`) and closed with it. See D1627.
// Should print 55.
function mk(): ((i32) => i32) | null { return (n: i32) => n + 1 }
const w = { f: mk() }
const v = w.f
if v != null { print(v(54)) }
